<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  What the controller artwork says, transcribed and nothing more.

  One <Game> per image. Each <Label> records the physical control the artwork draws a line
  to, and the text beside it, exactly as printed — including its spelling, its punctuation
  and its choice of words. No interpretation happens here: labels are not collapsed, not
  shortened, not corrected against the MAME controls database, and not mapped to emulator
  ports. Those are judgements, they belong downstream, and keeping them out means this file
  never has to be rebuilt when one of them changes.

  A control the artwork leaves unlabelled is simply absent. A directional cluster may carry
  one label for the whole control or one per direction; transcribe whichever is drawn.

  Control names are the plugin's own generic inputs, the same vocabulary Layout.xml uses:

      ButtonA ButtonB ButtonX ButtonY
      ButtonLeftShoulder ButtonRightShoulder AxisTriggerLeft AxisTriggerRight
      ButtonStart ButtonBack ButtonGuide ButtonLeftStick ButtonRightStick
      AxisLeftStick  AxisLeftStickUp/Down/Left/Right
      AxisRightStick AxisRightStickUp/Down/Left/Right
      ButtonDpad     ButtonDpadUp/Down/Left/Right

  Seeded by hand from images read during the import's measurement step. The remainder comes
  from the bulk read.
-->
